{"abstract":"The emergence of telepresence robots (TPRs) as mobile tools that can enable remote presence and interaction has been the focus of many endeavors that have provided insights on TPRs’ application in research, educational contexts, professional training, social inclusion and sense of embodiment. In this paper we have conducted semi-structured interviews with five individuals living abroad and one family member of a person living abroad to explore how TPRs can be employed to strengthen family ties and enhance the sense of presence in order to alleviate the emotional struggle that is often reported in these groups. Based on the participants’ responses we have showcased the relation between different technological features and communication, addressed concerns regarding the use of TPRs, and recognized activities that can be recreated remotely with the use of a TPR to potentially create an enhanced feeling of connection. The analysis presented could be the premise for subsequent implementation of TPRs in a way that is considered meaningful by people living in distance from their families.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Chatzipolakis, Pavlos","Yasuoka, Mika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820839"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Göteborg, se","start":"2025-06-22","title":"13th International Conference on Distributed, Ambient and Pervasive Interactions","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Family ties","Qualitative Research","Telepresence robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the potential of telepresence robots for individuals living abroad and their families a qualitative approach","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-820839","identifier":[{"id":"105007669615","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-8f41ac94-b7d4-498b-a4ff-b52af02eac13"],"keyword":["Family Ties","Qualitative Research","Telepresence Robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1E171C37B638F5B6211B9E2FC86A2C3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-05-26","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Pavlos","key":"chatzipolakispau","last":"Chatzipolakis","locid":"516027f6-7fba-4389-80e1-058b8e6cbecf","name":"Chatzipolakis, Pavlos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Mika","key":"yasuokajensenpau","last":"Yasuoka Jensen","locid":"1d987e7b-9820-43a1-9997-6c1e966654f6","name":"Yasuoka, Mika","name_org":"Yasuoka Jensen, Mika","orcid":"0000-0001-5209-7383","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Norbert A.","key":"streitzpedh","last":"Streitz","name":"Streitz, Norbert A.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shinichi","key":"konomipedh","last":"Konomi","name":"Konomi, Shinichi","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-92980-9_13","eisbn":["9783031929809"],"isbn":["9783031929793"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"203-215","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"13th International Conference, DAPI 2025, Held as Part of the 27th HCI International Conference, HCII 2025, Proceedings","title":"Distributed, Ambient and Pervasive Interactions","volume":"II"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007669615"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-8f41ac94-b7d4-498b-a4ff-b52af02eac13"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Exploring the Potential of Telepresence Robots for Individuals Living Abroad and Their Families : A Qualitative Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820839","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The use of digital tools inside the prisons has been deemed quintessential in highly digitized societies, to provide to the inmates premises for a better future upon their release, and to familiarize them with the use of everyday technologies. In this endeavor the authors have conducted qualitative research and applied Participatory Design approaches in the prison of Storstrøm, Denmark. The goal is to understand the current use of digital tools inside the facility, describe them and find possible struggles of the users and ways to tackle them. Upon the collection and analysis of the qualitative material various difficulties were discovered, connected with technical issues and sociopolitical factors. Design proposals and future digital implementations are being suggested, drawing from the ideas of Participatory Design, to facilitate the process of learning and reintegration for the prison population that wishes to pursue prospects for a better life after their release.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Chatzipolakis, Pavlos","Yasuoka, Mika","Georgoulakis,, Christos"],"cuid":["S02-087.40-793069"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-06","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2024-01-03","title":"57th Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences, HICSS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design","Digital tools","Participatory Design","Privacy","Qualitative methods","Security","prison education"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"to prove there is another way a qualitative study on digital tools for education in the storstrøm prison of denmark","src":["aau","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"f